WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.234
-The committee investigating

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.968
Donald Trump's attempted coup
on January 6th

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.801
held its first
televised hearing tonight

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:08.934
and, in advance of that hearing,

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.734
more audio emerged
of a phone call

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:14.234
in which House GOP Leader
Kevin McCarthy said, in the days

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:16.167
after the insurrection,
that there should be

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:18.000
an investigation
into what happened

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.767
and the people responsible
should be held accountable,

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.267
which is notable, of course,
since McCarthy,

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:22.567
like most of his fellow
Republicans,

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:25.400
have since changed their tune
to appease Trump.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.501
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:31.868
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:35.334
We do not know exactly what
happened at the hearing tonight

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.334
because we are taping this
before it airs,

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:40.334
but I'm hoping they really
jazzed it up for TV

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.601
and invited
some surprise guests.

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:45.801
-I want to now introduce
our witnesses today

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:46.868
and swear them in.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:47.901
Our first witness is...

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.901
-Rudy Giuliani!

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:53.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.267
-I'm guessing you could trick
Rudy Giuliani

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.667
into going anywhere
if you put him

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.000
in a jack-in-a-box
costume like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.334
One day we're going to see
federal agents carrying him

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.367
out of his apartment building
in that costume.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.901
[ As Giuliani ]
You guys promise we're going

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.367
to "America's Got Talent,"
right?

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.901
[ Laughter ]
In that case,

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.133
I'm going to crawl back
in my box

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.534
and go over the lyrics
to "Fireworks,"

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:11.901
so I don't embarrass myself.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:12.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:14.534
I'm guessing that didn't happen,
although,

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.133
we don't know for sure, since,

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:17.968
as of this taping,
we haven't seen the hearing,

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:19.467
which gives us something
in common

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:22.601
with viewers of Fox News,
which announced, in advance,

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:24.801
that it wouldn't be airing
the hearing live.

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:27.801
-Fox News making
a programing decision.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:30.667
It's sticking with its
primetime lineup on Thursday --

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.834
Tucker Carlson and Sean Hannity

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:33.934
This is instead of showing

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:36.100
the January 6th
Select Committee hearing

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.167
concerning
the Capitol Hill riot.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.767
-Of course, Fox isn't airing it.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.267
They're a key suspect in it.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:46.067
That would be like if Court TV's
coverage of the O.J. trial

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.934
had been hosted by O.J.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:50.367
"Whoops, sorry, fellas.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.901
The mic keeps slipping

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.133
out of these leather gloves,

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:54.434
which fit perfectly.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:55.567
[ Laughter ]
I mean, they're too small.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:58.334
Damn it! Cut!
No, not cut! Stop taping!

00:01:58.334 --> 00:01:59.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:04.133
Fox was an active participant

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.701
in spreading the big lie
that led to the attempted coup

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:09.968
and has since helped whitewash
and cover up what happened.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.334
In fact, the January 6th
Committee has already revealed

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:14.601
private texts from Fox hosts,
like Laura Ingraham,

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.767
Sean Hannity,
and Brian Kilmeade

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.934
to Trump Chief of Staff
Frank Meadows

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.234
on the day of the riot.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:21.701
Imagine if the committee
read those text messages

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:24.267
and then Fox cut back
to Hannity or Ingraham.

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.100
It'd be like watching
that "Planet Earth" clip

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.701
where the snakes
chase the iguana

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:30.634
and then, at the end, they cut
to an interview with the snakes.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:31.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.300
"Uh, look, I know it looks bad.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.033
We were just trying to,
I don't know, help the iguana.

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:37.100
Look, it's the food chain!"

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.467
In fact, we already know,

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.100
thanks to the
January 6th Committee,

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.901
not to take anything
Fox hosts state seriously,

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.534
since, behind the scenes,

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:48.100
they were privately imploring
Trump to quell the mob.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.734
They knew it was his fault

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.734
and they knew he had the power
to stop it.

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:55.667
They won't say that in public,
but they did say it in private.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:03:00.934
-Multiple Fox News hosts
knew the president needed

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:03.234
to act immediately.

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:08.934
They texted Mr. Meadows and he
has turned over those texts.

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:13.734
"Mark, the president needs
to tell people in the Capitol

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:15.501
to go home.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.501
This is hurting all of us

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:22.767
He is destroying his legacy,"
Laura Ingraham wrote.

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:25.701
"Please get him on tv.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:28.934
Destroying everything
you have accomplished,"

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:31.834
Brian Kilmeade texted.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:34.434
"Can he make a statement.

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:36.968
Ask people to leave
the capital,"

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.901
Sean Hannity urged.

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:40.200
-First of all,
I'm shocked to learn

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.367
that Brian Kilmeade
is capable of texting at all.

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:44.734
[ Laughter ]
I just assume he does
all is communicating

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:47.367
via a tin can
attached to a string.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:49.834
Second, and more importantly,
they all knew.

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:52.033
They said stuff like,
"This is hurting us all.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.000
Destroying his legacy.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.400
Can he ask people to leave?"

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.000
They were watching the ride
on TV, like the rest of us,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.767
and they all knew it was bad
and that Trump could stop it,

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:00.968
just like the rest of us.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:02.567
As you can see,
from these private texts,

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.067
they weren't sitting there,
thinking,

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:05.634
"This is just
a peaceful protest,"

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.400
or "This is all antifa's fault."

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.634
They knew Trump could stop it,
if he wanted to,

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:10.968
which makes them liars.

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:12.367
They don't even believe
their own bull[bleep].

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:15.167
In a way, it would at least
be more honest

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:16.801
if we found out that,
behind the scenes,

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.067
they were texting stuff like...

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:31.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:40.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.601 --> 00:05:01.000
And, by the way, they were not
the only Trump supporters

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.067
who were privately horrified
by the insurrection,

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:05.601
while publicly lying about it
or making excuses for it.

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:07.934
Just last night,
more bombshell audio

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:10.334
of GOP House Leader
Kevin McCarthy surfaced,

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.234
from the days
after the insurrection,

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.467
in which McCarthy was adamant

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:16.968
that there should be
a full investigation of the riot

00:05:16.968 --> 00:05:19.267
and that whoever was responsible
should be punished.

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:21.334
And he even went so far
as to tell

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:23.634
his fellow Republicans
on that call

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:25.934
that he had personally
confronted Trump.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:29.701
-Five days later,
McCarthy spoke to his members

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:31.667
and, again, it's on tape.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.934
McCarthy said that he got
on the phone,

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.734
he talked to Trump,
and that he castigated him

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:37.501
and he told him
to call off the mob.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.133
...was going on...

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.501
-I mean, I would imagine,
anytime you talk to Trump,

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:01.901
you have to be very loud
about it.

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:03.267
[ Laughter ]
The dude on the other end

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:04.501
of that phone call is so loud,

00:06:04.501 --> 00:06:06.334
he routinely did
his press conferences next

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.868
to a roaring helicopter
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.801
and we could still hear
every word he said.

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:13.801
[ Laughter ]
I mean, just look at his face.

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:15.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:15.434 --> 00:06:18.067
He always looks like
the villain in an action movie

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:21.133
who realizes the hero
has defused the bomb.

00:06:21.133 --> 00:06:23.133
[ As Trump ]
Damn you, Jean-Claude!

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:25.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.534
But even more revealing
than that part of the phone call

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:29.968
was the part where McCarthy
specifically went out of his way

00:06:29.968 --> 00:06:32.434
to insist that the events
of January 6th

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:34.534
deserve a full investigation

00:06:34.534 --> 00:06:36.801
and that the people responsible
should be held accountable.

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:39.934
-During that call,
McCarthy also is on tape vowing

00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:43.234
to make someone pay
for the attack,

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:45.000
even raising the idea

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.934
of a bipartisan commission
to investigate.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:59.167
-Strong words,
but then a few weeks later,

00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:00.400
he was at Mar-a-Lago,

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.033
posing for this photo
with Donald Trump,

00:07:02.033 --> 00:07:04.400
where they look like
rival strip club owners,

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.334
acting like nothing
ever happened.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.334 --> 00:07:09.400
He basically yada yada yada'd
an attempted coup.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.601
[ Laughter ]
On that phone call
you just heard,

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:12.968
just days
after the insurrection,

00:07:12.968 --> 00:07:14.033
he literally said the words,

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.467
"We can't sweep this
under the rug."

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:18.033
And now, he's essentially
showing up to all his interviews

00:07:18.033 --> 00:07:19.767
on Fox News
with a giant broom.

00:07:19.767 --> 00:07:22.067
[ Laughter ]
Also, side note here,

00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:23.868
but what is it with these guys
constantly

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:25.968
getting caught on tape
saying damning stuff?

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:27.701
Over the last six or so years,

00:07:27.701 --> 00:07:29.868
I've honestly lost count
of the number of times

00:07:29.868 --> 00:07:32.267
some Trump-adjacent doofus,
like Rudy or McCarthy,

00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:34.167
or Trump himself has been
caught on tape,

00:07:34.167 --> 00:07:36.300
directly contradicting something
they said in public.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.601
Next, we're going to find out
that, behind the scenes,

00:07:38.601 --> 00:07:40.667
Rudy Giuliani is actually
a very normal guy

00:07:40.667 --> 00:07:42.167
who never makes this face.

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.033
[ Laughter ]
And, yeah,

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:45.734
yeah, we use that photo a lot.

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:46.901
[ Laughter ]
But do you know --

00:07:46.901 --> 00:07:48.334
do you know what he's doing
in that photo?

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:49.968
He's taking a closer look.

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:52.334
[ Laughter ]

00:07:52.334 --> 00:07:53.834
That's where we got the idea.

00:07:53.834 --> 00:07:55.801
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah, we were like, "Oh."

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:57.234
[ Whistling ]

00:07:59.868 --> 00:08:02.534
Secret tapes are going to emerge
of Rudy doing normal stuff,

00:08:02.534 --> 00:08:04.667
like watching "Ozark"
or paying his cable bill

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:06.901
or checking into a hotel
looking like this.

00:08:06.901 --> 00:08:09.000
[ As Giuliani ] Hello.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.367
My name is Rudy Giuliani.

00:08:10.367 --> 00:08:12.667
I'm here to check in to the
actual Four Seasons Hotel,

00:08:12.667 --> 00:08:14.667
for a normal vacation
with my normal wife,

00:08:14.667 --> 00:08:16.968
who is not now,
nor has ever been, my cousin.

00:08:16.968 --> 00:08:18.934
[ Laughter ]
So, in private,

00:08:18.934 --> 00:08:20.701
McCarthy told
his fellow Republicans

00:08:20.701 --> 00:08:22.400
the coup attempt couldn't be
swept under the rug.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.834
Now, he's doing exactly that,
going on Fox

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:26.334
and trying to sweep it
under the rug

00:08:26.334 --> 00:08:28.701
by slamming the investigation
as illegitimate

00:08:28.701 --> 00:08:30.601
and claiming it shouldn't
even be happening.

00:08:30.601 --> 00:08:32.501
-What they're doing
in this committee

00:08:32.501 --> 00:08:35.434
is going after their
political foes, their opponents.

00:08:35.434 --> 00:08:37.200
We've watched it time and again.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.667
What we have found,
with one-party rule

00:08:39.667 --> 00:08:42.601
of Democrats taking over
the House, the Senate,

00:08:42.601 --> 00:08:43.901
and the presidency,

00:08:43.901 --> 00:08:47.501
they use the power to go
after their political opponents,

00:08:47.501 --> 00:08:50.033
instead of bringing down
gasoline prices.

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:53.968
Today, it has now doubled,
the gasoline price,

00:08:53.968 --> 00:08:55.968
since President Biden
has taken office.

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:57.968
Are they going to have
any hearings on that?

00:08:57.968 --> 00:09:00.300
-They always do this annoying
thing where they're like,

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.067
"People care more
about gas prices."

00:09:02.067 --> 00:09:03.801
You know we're all capable
of caring

00:09:03.801 --> 00:09:05.701
about more than one thing
at a time, right?

00:09:05.701 --> 00:09:07.734
[ Laughter ]
I think people can focus

00:09:07.734 --> 00:09:09.167
on an attack on democracy.

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:10.334
I mean, what else
are they going to do?

00:09:10.334 --> 00:09:11.400
They can't drive anywhere

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.868
because gas is
so [bleep] expensive.

00:09:12.868 --> 00:09:14.400
[ Laughter and applause ]
But,

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.234
McCarthy's opposition
to the investigation

00:09:16.234 --> 00:09:17.868
is also self-interested,
since he was

00:09:17.868 --> 00:09:19.367
personally subpoenaed
by the committee

00:09:19.367 --> 00:09:21.634
and he told Fox that he
responded to that subpoena

00:09:21.634 --> 00:09:23.067
with a bunch of questions.

00:09:23.067 --> 00:09:26.000
-Did you receive a subpoena
from the January 6th Committee

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.367
and, if so, how did you respond?

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:31.734
-I did receive a subpoena
and I requested --

00:09:31.734 --> 00:09:33.167
I asked for information.

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:37.200
Eleven pages, I sent a letter
to this committee.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.167
I sent a letter to this
committee a year ago,

00:09:39.167 --> 00:09:41.901
when they asked to talk to me,
and they never responded.

00:09:41.901 --> 00:09:43.601
-Probably because your questions
were super dumb.

00:09:43.601 --> 00:09:45.501
I mean, I'm just guessing.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.501 --> 00:09:47.000
But I'm pretty confident
that they were super dumb.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.868
It's like when you invite
your friends to a party

00:09:48.868 --> 00:09:51.133
and most people just RSVP,
but then one guy writes back...

00:09:54.734 --> 00:09:57.400
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.434
"Also, does your house
have European outlets,

00:09:59.434 --> 00:10:00.634
or should I bring converters?"

00:10:00.634 --> 00:10:02.534
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:03.901
Also, you're obviously entitled

00:10:03.901 --> 00:10:06.200
to ask whatever questions
you want, but, ultimately,

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:07.934
it's a subpoena.
You have to comply.

00:10:07.934 --> 00:10:09.901
Although, maybe not anymore?

00:10:09.901 --> 00:10:12.767
It does feel like this committee
is pretty easy to say no to.

00:10:12.767 --> 00:10:15.033
The Justice Department just
announced they won't even charge

00:10:15.033 --> 00:10:17.434
two former Trump aides
with contempt of Congress

00:10:17.434 --> 00:10:18.968
for refusing to cooperate.

00:10:18.968 --> 00:10:21.667
They react the way I do when I'm
trying to get my kids to eat.

00:10:21.667 --> 00:10:23.467
Finish your pasta!
"I don't want to!"

00:10:23.467 --> 00:10:25.968
Great! Then I guess
you'll just go hungry!

00:10:25.968 --> 00:10:28.667
Why don't you go think about it
while you play video games?!

00:10:28.667 --> 00:10:29.734
Yeah. Alright.

00:10:29.734 --> 00:10:31.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.634
And when Republicans
aren't actively

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:37.100
obstructing the investigation,
they're claiming

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.133
no one's going to watch
because people would rather

00:10:39.133 --> 00:10:40.901
spend their time
doing other things.

00:10:40.901 --> 00:10:42.667
-This is not
a fact-finding mission.

00:10:42.667 --> 00:10:45.601
This is a two-hour,
free documentary sponsored

00:10:45.601 --> 00:10:47.567
by virtually every
major network in America,

00:10:47.567 --> 00:10:48.467
except for this one,

00:10:48.467 --> 00:10:49.734
that's willing to give it
airtime.

00:10:49.734 --> 00:10:51.033
The only good thing about it is

00:10:51.033 --> 00:10:52.834
most Americans aren't going
to watch this garbage.

00:10:52.834 --> 00:10:54.934
Okay, so the question --
does it work?

00:10:54.934 --> 00:10:57.367
Do people watch?

00:10:57.367 --> 00:10:59.100
-Well, I'd be interested to see

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:00.167
what the ratings
are going to be.

00:11:00.167 --> 00:11:01.300
This is kind of like watching --

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.767
Are they're going to go watch
"Top Gun,"

00:11:02.767 --> 00:11:04.968
which is entertainment,
or are they going to watch

00:11:04.968 --> 00:11:08.968
the J6, you know,
TV-produced show?

00:11:08.968 --> 00:11:10.934
-Again, you know,
it's not an either/or, right?

00:11:10.934 --> 00:11:13.267
You can watch "Top Gun"
and the hearing.

00:11:13.267 --> 00:11:14.901
You don't have to pick one.

00:11:14.901 --> 00:11:16.767
It's not like people are
showing up to the movie theaters

00:11:16.767 --> 00:11:19.033
and the only two choices
at the ticket counter are...

00:11:19.033 --> 00:11:22.200
[ Laughter ]

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:25.567
Although, I will say, you got
to see the hearings on IMAX.

00:11:25.567 --> 00:11:26.367
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.367 --> 00:11:27.467
That's what everybody --

00:11:27.467 --> 00:11:30.334
You haven't experienced
true cinema,

00:11:30.334 --> 00:11:33.100
until you've seen a close-up
of Rudy Giuliani's teeth

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.000
on a 52-foot IMAX screen.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:35.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:35.834 --> 00:11:36.634
Uhhh!

00:11:36.634 --> 00:11:38.400
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:39.100
"Anybody --

00:11:43.033 --> 00:11:44.868
Anybody want the rest
of my Raisinettes?"

00:11:44.868 --> 00:11:47.601
[ Laughter ]
Also, can we go back to this?

00:11:47.601 --> 00:11:50.367
-This is a two-hour,
free documentary sponsored

00:11:50.367 --> 00:11:52.601
by virtually every
major network in America.

00:11:52.601 --> 00:11:55.434
-Oh, now, you're suddenly
against TV networks

00:11:55.434 --> 00:11:57.033
giving one side free airtime?

00:11:57.033 --> 00:11:58.467
I don't seem to remember
you objecting

00:11:58.467 --> 00:12:01.133
when Fox aired Trump's
marathon rallies live

00:12:01.133 --> 00:12:03.601
or when he used to call in
to "Fox &amp; Friends" once a week

00:12:03.601 --> 00:12:06.267
and just scream whatever
the hell he wanted unchallenged

00:12:06.267 --> 00:12:07.534
[ Laughter ]
for an entire hour,

00:12:07.534 --> 00:12:09.300
while the hosts just sat there
on the couch

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:11.067
with blank stares
on their faces,

00:12:11.067 --> 00:12:13.968
[ Laughter ]
like "Jeopardy!" contestants
getting a question

00:12:13.968 --> 00:12:16.467
about rap lyrics.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:16.467 --> 00:12:17.901
Again, we don't know
exactly what happened

00:12:17.901 --> 00:12:19.667
in this hearing tonight
because we're taping beforehand,

00:12:19.667 --> 00:12:21.801
but we do know some of the most
important stuff already,

00:12:21.801 --> 00:12:23.901
which is that Donald Trump was
at the center

00:12:23.901 --> 00:12:25.968
of an attempted coup
to overturn American democracy

00:12:25.968 --> 00:12:27.334
and remain in power

00:12:27.334 --> 00:12:29.400
as an unelected tyrant
against the will of the people.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.434
He pulled the strings
and his fellow Republicans,

00:12:31.434 --> 00:12:33.901
including his friends on Fox,
knew what he was doing,

00:12:33.901 --> 00:12:35.067
they knew it was wrong,

00:12:35.067 --> 00:12:36.367
and they knew he had
the power to stop it.

00:12:36.367 --> 00:12:38.701
Kevin McCarthy even went
out of his way to say

00:12:38.701 --> 00:12:41.000
that this can't be swept
under the rug.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.767
They said that
about the insurrection,

00:12:42.767 --> 00:12:44.534
the same thing everyone
in the audience

00:12:44.534 --> 00:12:45.868
at "The Masked Singer" said
when they heard

00:12:45.868 --> 00:12:47.834
Rudy Giuliani's singing voice,
which is...

00:12:47.834 --> 00:12:49.367
-This is hurting all of us.

00:12:49.367 --> 00:12:50.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

